+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+# Request
+
+Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service: it cancels the booking at the time `at` and returns
+`{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount given back to the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its
+equipment, and a booking can only be cancelled once.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- Refund follows the school's cancellation policy (task-001): no refund when `at` is less than 24h before the
+  booking's start (or later), otherwise the full booking total, in integer cents.
+- `at` is an ISO-8601 UTC string; otherwise `cancel` throws. An unknown booking id throws.
+- A cancelled booking frees its item for new bookings and availability; cancelling twice throws.
+- Tests under `node --test`.
